---
// The privacy page (spec story 91): plain words, names Cloudflare, lists what the form stores
// and the retention limits. The day counts come from the code that enforces them.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import TopBar from "../components/TopBar.astro";
import { DECLINED_KEPT_MS, EMAIL_KEPT_MS } from "../submissions/store.ts";

const DAY = 86_400_000;
const emailDays = EMAIL_KEPT_MS / DAY;
const declinedDays = DECLINED_KEPT_MS / DAY;
---

<Base title="Privacy · AstraTron" description="What AstraTron keeps about you, where, and for how long.">
  <TopBar />
  <main class="page prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      AstraTron has no accounts, no ads and no analytics. We don't count visits, set tracking cookies or send anything about you to
      advertisers. Here is everything that happens to what you do and send.
    </p>

    <h2>Your progress stays in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      Your Lesson progress, your Streak and your theme and motion choices are saved in this browser's local storage. They never leave
      your device unless you export them to a file yourself. Clearing your browser's site data deletes them.
    </p>

    <h2>Who runs the servers: Cloudflare</h2>
    <p>
      AstraTron is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, and the form's entries are kept in a Cloudflare database. Like any web host,
      Cloudflare sees your IP address when it delivers a page; AstraTron doesn't keep it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to stop spam without a puzzle. To tell people from bots, Turnstile looks at your IP address and
      browser details on Cloudflare's side, under <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>. Only
      a pass or fail comes back to AstraTron; none of those details are stored with your entry.
    </p>

    <h2>What the form stores</h2>
    <p>When you suggest a Problem or report a mistake, we store only what you type or pick:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>whether it's a Problem or a mistake report, and the Unit;</li>
      <li>for a mistake report, which Step or Problem it's about;</li>
      <li>the Problem text (or what's wrong) and your answer and reasoning;</li>
      <li>a molecule, if you give one;</li>
      <li>a display name, if you give one, used as the credit on an accepted Problem (otherwise "a Student");</li>
      <li>a reply email, if you give one, used for at most one reply;</li>
      <li>your licence consent (an accepted Problem is published under CC BY-NC-SA <span class="data">4.0</span>);</li>
      <li>where your entry is in review, and the dates it was sent, decided and replied to.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We store no IP address, no browser details, no cookies and no account data. Entries are never posted publicly or turned into
      public issues. Please don't put personal info, like your full name, school or phone number, in your text.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Your reply email is deleted as soon as the one reply is sent, or after <span class="data">{emailDays}</span> days if no reply is
        sent.
      </li>
      <li>
        A Problem or report we turn down, or screen out, is deleted <span class="data">{declinedDays}</span> days after that decision.
      </li>
      <li>An accepted Problem's entry is deleted once the Problem is published; only the published Problem, with your credit, remains.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Donations</h2>
    <p>
      Donate goes to Ko-fi, a separate site. Anything you give Ko-fi is covered by Ko-fi's own privacy policy; AstraTron gets no payment
      details.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
